text.section:
Any district created pursuant to this chapter may be abolished by resolutions passed by the governing body and the town council of any participating town, upon the joint petition of the commission and the owners of at least 51 percent of the land area located within the district. Joint petitions shall:

State whether the purposes for which the district was formed have been substantially achieved;


State whether all obligations incurred by the district have been fully paid;


Describe the benefits that can be expected from the abolition of the district; and


Request the governing body to abolish the district.
